      "writtenOn": "2021-01-21T20:56:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003ePerhaps we should keep things as they are internally, but also add convenience getExcludedRoutes() and getUnicastRoutes(), and advise users to use these?\n\nWill `getExcludedRoutes` and `getUnicastRoutes` methods be actually useful?\nDon\u0027t we have to look at all routes to see the full picture?\n\nAs an example:\nLet\u0027s say a certain destination is covered by one of the routes returned by `getUnicastRoutes`.\nThis actually doesn\u0027t tell us anything, because there might be more specific RTN_THROW or RTN_UNREACHABLE route. And we need to call `getExcludedRoutes` to check that.",
      "parentUuid": "b9b667e7_11db006d",
      "revId": "9ef500cc102ca5a797338bf3e8f10aa8b0e94696",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "52463d24_f1da1aa3",
