      "writtenOn": "2021-01-20T16:19:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After thinking about this change for a bit, I\u0027m actually not sure this is what we want. Even for advanced users, I think there is is the long term potential for confusion or bugs if we include throw routes in getRoutes like this. I wonder if it would be better to add a separate getExcludedRoutes method that returns only the throw routes?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 766,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 772,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "9ef500cc102ca5a797338bf3e8f10aa8b0e94696",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7620d60e_6a4be79f",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/LinkProperties.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 772,
      "author": {
        "id": 1725373
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-01-21T20:56:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Adding separate `getExcludedRoutes` method and return only unicast routes in `getRoutes` is possible. (We\u0027ll need to also add something like `getAllExcludedRoutes` as a counterpart to `getAllRoutes`)\n\nBut I think this might encourage clients to simply ignore those excluded routes. This will lead to incorrect behavior in some cases.\nTo handle excluded routes correctly clients will need to always call both `getRoutes` and `getExcludedRoutes` anyway.\n\nHaving one method that returns all routes will be more convenient and will encourage clients not to ignore excluded routes.\n\nAlso, since throw routes in `getRoutes` are gated on target sdk S, documentation for S will mention this change and app developers will be aware of this.",
      "parentUuid": "0495c078_091117d1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 766,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 772,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "9ef500cc102ca5a797338bf3e8f10aa8b0e94696",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
